{"agent":"close-bldupes","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`bug_duplicate` does not validate whether the duplicate bug (`bug`) is already closed by another mechanism (e.g., already closed as invalid or fixed independently) before trying to close it. If `bug` is already closed, `bug_invalid` is called on it again, appending a duplicate resolution event to an already closed bug, which corrupts the event log state and contradicts the docstring's claim that it is refused.","digest":"c3aac591c9805ad6","family":"google","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:44","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:44"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`open_duplicates` treats `duplicate_of` as undirected. The inbound scan is correct (`other` lists `bug` in `duplicate_of`, so `other` is the duplicate). `found |= own.linked(\"duplicate_of\")` then adds the originals this bug claims to duplicate. Given D linked `duplicate_of` O, D still open, and `bug fixed D` (own regression test), the fold lists O. `knowledge.py` then tells the operator to run `bug duplicate O --of D`. After D is `resolution == \"fixed\"` with a test, `bug_duplicate` accepts that and `bug_invalid`s the original. Links written by `bug_duplicate` itself (`link_record(repo, bug, \"duplicate_of\", of)`) only need the inbound scan; the outbound union inverts the edge.","digest":"9615d13cbb3da51c","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:29","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:29"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12338,"diff_sha":"fc33f57a117d94dceecd9936690578ddb6a23a4e9849eff22ccf080680f89d8c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/B-dup-closure","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":60.5,"family":"google","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"bb8e16edf66f338c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/B-dup-closure.critic.grok-4.7.20261111T104054Z-0d4927c5.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"ba85784117ac4b4f77a74141e026880d703bf28f","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/knowledge/__init__.py":"100644 250a4bbb052e25e561a3570c9b6c9c086e772a29","ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py":"100644 6eaa39442f194d9ba3f12a8897faa4dcc3e6a6d6","ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py":"100644 c95a26c04aa13f4042eadb565cd90cd17c0b6b14","ddflow/surfaces/commands/knowledge.py":"100644 4faa5a47f88a1b6aa700696090cd8be88817546a","ddflow/surfaces/declared/records.py":"100644 f9dc431bc751d697f4c2d95f5a1a47439b8d4076","tests/test_dup_closure.py":"100644 e7e5c2113f4343ce7f9db8fe121bb2276b2ef0d0"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:44","ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_duplicate.py:29"],"tree_sha":"ba85784117ac+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e796d8d387d19b8b57568c07f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":173043,"schema":1,"subject":"B-dup-closure","ts":"2026-11-11T10:41:55.719587Z"}
